# Dedicated installed session CLI acceptance

Freeze the clean CLI source 0d262a8acc237bba2d7b1f3ef87b8fa23b911f7c.
Keep the 8f4dd72c workspace client, its hash and handoff immutable.

Primary sources:
- The published identity contract and registered browser_sessions.go handler:
  list is scoped to the authenticated account and entrance. DELETE sends no
  body/query, uses CSRF, and clears identity cookies for the caller's own session.
- Identity.RevokeBrowserSession writes auth.logout on target_type=session.
  The target UUID is the affected session. An acknowledged retry adds no second event.
- The audit public operation already filters by actor, action, target and outcome.
- https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/viewing-and-managing-your-sessions
- https://pkg.go.dev/runtime/debug#BuildInfo
- https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/ssl.html
- https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/subprocess.html
- https://docs.python.org/3.12/license.html

Use only a fixture-owner-issued pair of dedicated disposable platform-admin
accounts, with an exclusive fixture ID and protected file references. Reject
the installation's bootstrap email and every declared DEL/OBS/Web protected
identity before authentication. Recheck the live Me identity after each fresh
login before any cleanup or session mutation. No fallback administrator exists.

Create only fresh private CLI profiles. Track only the current session produced
by each successful login in this run. Successful revocation is restricted to
that run-created registry and the same canary account/entrance. Foreign-account
and Portal targets are also new canary sessions, never existing shared sessions.
Do not revoke an arbitrary ID obtained from a list or fixture input.

Qualify owned-session revocation, idempotent retry, self-revocation/local cleanup,
new-login recovery, foreign-account and cross-entrance refusal, live survival
of each refused target and public audit readback. Storage/transport uncertainty
remains covered by the committed race/TLS protocol tests; do not fault the shared
database or add a proxy to force an installed failure. Label this boundary.

Source, image and binary evidence for Control come from the actual DEL installed
provenance. CLI source/build-info/hash are independent. Use only the original
installed window, actual CA/origins and its network PID. Join its network
namespace; isolate hostname mapping in a new private mount namespace. Do not
start a server, database, container, account lifecycle or second installation.

Existing CLI dependencies and notices remain as reviewed in docs/research/cli.md.
The driver uses only Python 3.12 standard library, under the PSF licence.
Go is BSD-3-Clause and Cobra Apache-2.0. These permit commercial/offline use and
redistribution under their notices. No new dependency, model or dataset is added.

Guard tests must refuse shared identities, fixture/source mismatch, unsafe
credentials, unowned/pre-existing targets and source substitution. Those tests,
a build or help run are not an installed end-to-end result.
